 ### SCENARIO-PHASE4-4424: Exp4424 Either Reproduces One Deeper sc25 Level Or Reports Mechanic-Test Partial
 **Description:** Running Exp 4424 either writes `success: sc25_L2_offline_reproduced` when the selected `sc25` target reproduces one level beyond its registry prior best through the offline reproduction gate, or writes `complete: sc25_L2_hud_cleanup_fixed_reproduction_gap` when the L2 first-cast HUD-cleanup transition test passes but the target L2 reproduction still does not. A valid artifact MUST set `offline_reproduced` as a bare bool, `reproduced_levels` as a bare int, `verifier_is_oracle=true`, preserve `honest_verdict` as a terminal-prefixed string, record `prior_best_level` and `target_level`, include `per_mechanic_tests` with independent pass/fail rows, include `residual_failing_mechanic` on partials, and compute `reproducibility_checksum` from the selected target, patched world model, unit-test path, reproduction result, residual gap, and random seed.
+
+### REQ-PHASE4-4477: ARC-AGI-3 Per-Game Online Discriminative Frontier Pruning
+**Description:** The live `StepwiseExplorer` SHALL collect frame-only online weak labels during search: non-terminal graph states as per-game on-frontier positives and game-over/off-path child frames as negatives. Once both classes are present, it SHALL fit a per-game `DiscriminativeVerifier` from `arc_value_learner.py` without using cross-game labels, score frontier states by `P(on-path)`, and prune states below the configured probability floor before the steps-to-go value head routes the remaining frontier.
+
+The terminal artifact `results/experiment_4477_per_game_online_discriminative.json` MUST compare the online-discriminative explorer against the bare explorer on held-out offline ARC game fixtures at equal frame-only action budget. It MUST include top-level fields `honest_verdict`, `inference_substrate`, `offline_reproduced`, `reproduced_levels`, `preconditions_checked`, `baseline_solve_rate`, `online_solve_rate`, `solve_rate_delta`, `baseline_actions_to_first_levelup`, `online_actions_to_first_levelup`, `actions_to_first_levelup_delta`, `per_game_results`, `online_verifier`, `random_seed`, `reproducibility_checksum`, `submitted_to_leaderboard`, `field_principles`, and `spec_refs`. The required field principles SHALL include: `honest_verdict` terminal-prefix discipline; `inference_substrate` explicit declaration from `{live_llm_inference, verifier_ensemble_against_cached_candidates, aggregation_from_upstream_artifacts}`; `offline_reproduced` counting only offline-reproducible solves; `reproduced_levels` as the real-env-confirmed banked count; and `preconditions_checked` naming the resources verified before launch.
+
+### SCENARIO-PHASE4-4477: Online Discriminative Negatives Prune Low-Probability Frontier States
+**Description:** Given a `StepwiseExplorer` instance for one game, when exploration observes at least one alive frame and at least one game-over/off-path frame, then the explorer trains a per-game online `DiscriminativeVerifier`, records positive and negative sample counts, annotates frontier states with `P(on-path)`, and excludes a low-probability frontier state before selecting the next action. Running Exp 4477 MUST either write `success: per_game_online_discriminative_improves_solve_rate` when held-out solve rate increases, `complete: per_game_online_discriminative_no_solve_rate_gain` when the equal-budget comparison does not improve solve rate, or `complete: per_game_online_discriminative_blocked_<resource>` when offline fixtures or imports are missing. A valid artifact MUST use `inference_substrate="verifier_ensemble_against_cached_candidates"`, MUST keep `submitted_to_leaderboard=false`, and MUST NOT set `offline_reproduced=true` unless an offline reproduction gate actually banks at least one level.
